    "media:imagetext": "gulf (where Naoirthur was to wake a eomewhat more important landing\nin later yeara) to refuel.\nOur flying time, as I recall, was about\n8 hours.\nManila has grow into a aprawling community of three million\npeople.\nSun. Dec. 20 He 3ook off for Quan, Hake, Honolulu, a total 06 5,300\nmiles. In Manila the PAA/l and his wife took uf to a series of parties\nevery night. Al1 their Irlende were very kand to include us and as\nmost of the affairs were large I guess a couple of more didn't maice\nsoo much difference.\nle saw lota of old Indends. The party ve enjoyed\nthe post was coolstails for just un and the Oppenheimera (PAA#1) given\nby General and Mrs. Carlos Romilo at their beautiful home on the out-\nskirts of Manila.\nHe has heid many important posts such as Philippine\nAmbassador to the U.S. and more important President of the General\nAssembly of the United Nations. You old China Hands will laugh when\nI tell you that for small chow we had among other things Quall eggs.\nPersonally I'd rather eat f 'em \u0026 your or two later after they have\nbecome birds. Romulo, you will remember was with MacArthur on Corrigidor\nand wrote a best seller wich I think was called \"I San the Pall of the\nPhilippines\" or something like that. In his study he has autographed\npictures of four or five Presidents and most of the crowned beads of\nthe world and a whole case full of decorations. He was the speaker\nat the 150th commencement of Washington University in Sto Louis and\nwas given a degree by Ethan Shepley. He is now President of the\nUniversity of the Philippines.\nHe and his wife are most charming\npeople. After ve got to Honolulu one of the papers carried the piece\nwhich I enclose.\nIn his five points Romulo expresses iy own convictions\nfar better than I am able to do. I think you wilà agree that it is\nworth reading.\nThis morning wille Debby packed I took a ride on a Hydrofoil bost\nfrom in front of the Manila Hotel to our old sea plane base at Cavite.\nWe made the round trip in an hour at a speed of about 40 miles per\nbout.\nWith a full load of 70 passengers both ways. One interesting\nthing about Manila is that none of the newspapers, there are several,\npublishes any daily weather information. Why should they. The weather\nis alwaya the same 80-90 eroept if there ia a typhoon hovering avaund.\nThat is well publicized. To my mind a sad development has been the\nacceptance of Tagabog as the offiolal language. This is simply a very\nstupid expression of nationalism.\nThey are turning their baoks on the\nwealth oi Ingliad and Spanish literature to adopt a language only\nrecently reduced to writing with no back ground whatever.\nle left Manila at 2130 Sunday afternoon, Deo. 20, and now as I write\nthis ve have just landed at Wake 3,000 to the east.\nIt is now 2 a.1.\nSunday morning Dec. 20th. and we are scheduled to arrive Hondlulu 5,300\nmiles from Manila some four or five hours earlier than our take-off, due\nof oourse to orosaing the Date Line.\nLater, Tues. Deo. 22.\nThe hotel situation at this time of year in\nHonolulu is really tough because 2 constantly increasing number of\nMainlanders come here for Christmas. PAA booked us in a brand new\nhotel on Walkiki beach called the Kalmana. It is between Diamond\nHead and the wide blue Pacific.\nOur 6th floor room has a small\nrom which we view the whole of the Beach. The weather has not pard\n\u0026 SSLISIPIOS",
